# Default: every file git auto-detects as text is normalized to LF in the
# index AND checked out LF, whatever the local core.autocrlf. This closes the
# Windows-git vs WSL-git divergence (the same bytes read as "clean" on one
# side and "~45 modified" on the other after a CRLF smudge — audit Fable5
# BUILD-02). Binary-looking files (e.g. docs/dashboard/index.html with its
# inlined assets) keep git's auto-detection and are left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binaries — never normalized, never diffed as text.
*.pgo binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary

# Normalise les fins de ligne des sources Go en LF dans le depot (index),
# quelle que soit la config core.autocrlf locale. Elimine les faux positifs
# gofmt (86 fichiers signales en 1:1) cotes contributeurs Windows ou le
# working tree est en CRLF mais l'index en LF gofmt-propre (A4-10).
*.go text eol=lf

# Les scripts shell doivent rester en LF dans le working tree meme sous
# core.autocrlf=true : bash (y compris via WSL sur /mnt/c) echoue sur les \r
# CRLF ("syntax error near unexpected token `$'{\r''"). Sans cette regle,
# scripts/check.sh est checkout en CRLF sur Windows et n'est pas executable.
*.sh text eol=lf
